* Participation status.
B. Daily Transactions
* Date.
* Vendor.
* Paid transactions.
* Prepaid servings created.
* Free servings redeemed.
C. Rice Bank
* Opening balance.
* New credits.
* Redemptions.
* Closing balance.
D. Public Dashboard
* Citywide prepaid servings.
* Citywide redemptions.
* Current outstanding balance.
* Community Goal progress.
* Participating vendors.
Essential accounting rule
The project must distinguish:
* Money received by a vendor.
* Prepaid servings outstanding.
* Servings actually redeemed.
A prepaid serving is a commitment that must be honoured.
At the beginning, each serving is redeemable at the same vendor where it was purchased. This prevents cross-vendor payment disputes.
Cross-vendor redemption may be introduced in a later version using a central clearing and reimbursement system.
