16. Final Strategic Recommendation
Start with a citywide campaign identity but a decentralized operational structure.
Do not build an app, kitchen or complicated donation platform.
Use existing vendors, existing customers, a shared Community Goal and transparent accounting.
The first 30 days should prove three things:
1. Ordinary customers are willing to pay for one additional serving.
2. Vendors can manage prepaid servings without financial losses or accounting discrepancies.
3. People actually redeem the free servings.
If these three conditions are demonstrated, Rice Circle can expand without needing to build an expensive new food distribution infrastructure.
The ultimate objective is to make giving one extra serving of rice a normal part of everyday life in Dumaguete.